[{:db/id "q-105644/selection/6a1d4a3e281f54eee662440aff1d500ff4f5b097ad253960f61427bb5ede0563" :answer/id #uuid "a17d4504-7689-5a47-abbf-4d20d21cdf1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6y+6x-3{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105644/selection/327af2c8bcd854f6a9760362f2d46578a3349c41844d5f0f06d1e6eb852c133c" :answer/id #uuid "545c3b77-5097-5e8e-a720-46d86fc41262" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2y+2x-9{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105644/selection/67c61f618220de15df7c7271ce4cfac69095f909335dec3a6216205b093fed0c" :answer/id #uuid "c71b1581-fbc2-5646-ab0f-5371361bc234" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6x-9{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105644/selection/9af39a1f418bc76ea71393a36b78e987d237643cfa4e56f84aea21c937f2e047" :answer/id #uuid "88a6805d-0f9f-57ec-ac59-3d46e90c2f2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9x-9{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105644/selection/3cf5c4cd5d7c76e83be354a173bf334823d9a321779a3d749dcccc56761fab0b" :answer/id #uuid "671fd369-287b-5129-8a8a-ee831f1593a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6x-3{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105644/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1a461ae2-73ae-5180-8485-dc11d5362c39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105644/selection/67c61f618220de15df7c7271ce4cfac69095f909335dec3a6216205b093fed0c" :answer-field/choices ["q-105644/selection/6a1d4a3e281f54eee662440aff1d500ff4f5b097ad253960f61427bb5ede0563" "q-105644/selection/327af2c8bcd854f6a9760362f2d46578a3349c41844d5f0f06d1e6eb852c133c" "q-105644/selection/67c61f618220de15df7c7271ce4cfac69095f909335dec3a6216205b093fed0c" "q-105644/selection/9af39a1f418bc76ea71393a36b78e987d237643cfa4e56f84aea21c937f2e047" "q-105644/selection/3cf5c4cd5d7c76e83be354a173bf334823d9a321779a3d749dcccc56761fab0b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105644" :question/id #uuid "f0ae3676-c659-57d6-821a-90fe5e47cb07" :question/math-academy-id "q-105644" :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\cdot (3F)$ for the vector field $F$ where\n\n$$\nF=(2yx+{x}^{2})\\,i+(5-{y}^{3})\\,j-2yz\\,k.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (3F)=3∇\\cdot F.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2yx+{x}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(5-{y}^{3})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(-2yz) \\\\  & =2y+2x-3{y}^{2}-2y \\\\  & =2x-3{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (3F) & =3∇\\cdot F \\\\  & =3(2x-3{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =6x-9{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-105644/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "78adaeaa-a91e-53e2-a192-1440d4d41211"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105644"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105642/selection/cdb509f459cf547f910ded690b5b8fbbb4d07ad783a9a8a96cc0e35df0459c1c" :answer/id #uuid "f97dc7a2-93d2-51b8-8658-43d0c5967214" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2y(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105642/selection/3b0bda3e66b34bcbbcd7fd99c74600d6a1d6a5b5c9210d7965533b312fa1a4e8" :answer/id #uuid "af84fbfd-cdc4-5f5e-927e-835f46abcef2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105642/selection/f58c60f349bf5f4b83ed2f503e1592f46354b611aba6db804d8f61add1b750d0" :answer/id #uuid "a6b3b928-47c8-5f4c-a1c5-b1b44607f6ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105642/selection/8b7ca526475ccd62caa65d95bea1fc1a6d79c2a9416b034377193757519b86ae" :answer/id #uuid "d9aa8855-00bd-5891-a89e-f3acf47db1ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2y(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105642/selection/9b23b3f2b83b1d86d92eeb89ed0436551b0ccaee4c7db98200be83c991492d75" :answer/id #uuid "47c4a8e0-3238-522a-b8af-61b8757de96a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105642/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "458e684b-531d-5491-9565-c22bbd87c191" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105642/selection/f58c60f349bf5f4b83ed2f503e1592f46354b611aba6db804d8f61add1b750d0" :answer-field/choices ["q-105642/selection/cdb509f459cf547f910ded690b5b8fbbb4d07ad783a9a8a96cc0e35df0459c1c" "q-105642/selection/3b0bda3e66b34bcbbcd7fd99c74600d6a1d6a5b5c9210d7965533b312fa1a4e8" "q-105642/selection/f58c60f349bf5f4b83ed2f503e1592f46354b611aba6db804d8f61add1b750d0" "q-105642/selection/8b7ca526475ccd62caa65d95bea1fc1a6d79c2a9416b034377193757519b86ae" "q-105642/selection/9b23b3f2b83b1d86d92eeb89ed0436551b0ccaee4c7db98200be83c991492d75"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105642" :question/id #uuid "0be2ffe8-e9dc-50a3-800e-03dd47a6055c" :question/math-academy-id "q-105642" :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\cdot (F+G)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,i-{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,j,\\,∇\\cdot G=2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)) \\\\  & =-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) \\\\  & =-4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (F+G) & =∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G \\\\  & =-4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) \\\\  & =-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105642/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "78adaeaa-a91e-53e2-a192-1440d4d41211"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105642"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105640/selection/03da036926b8683a78d859bd5f9a652e7ef6f8083aa853853969df1fb1286c54" :answer/id #uuid "1d8b7c48-14a3-58ea-9de0-a780cb2fa5ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7{e}^{5x}+3{e}^{3y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105640/selection/541c51de94eca33dd95cb7f04cf4709a4b64a8774e7bf00da6cd38271004edfc" :answer/id #uuid "bb55f415-b60c-553d-bfc8-1fef29d9c0c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13{e}^{5x}+4{e}^{3y}+6y{e}^{3y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105640/selection/934173d437db32c5d1d10a5eaea13370839cf0031a002c20f9db6fb2f0aefe40" :answer/id #uuid "3f364201-86de-5848-b248-cb8abc348f00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13{e}^{5x}+6y{e}^{3y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105640/selection/2cb876cf503485a55a0b4f0b4e5b3b54e8dd9ba62cbe32db7b046f0087139d2e" :answer/id #uuid "af59390d-7514-5a6d-934f-13e72bc97f03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13{e}^{5x}+3{e}^{3y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105640/selection/0745f78343ab533087b71a60da3b79665cbfe6415b311709535e9e6adf213ebf" :answer/id #uuid "421219d4-02f9-5546-99ed-adaee55f971a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7{e}^{5x}-4{e}^{3y}+6y{e}^{3y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105640/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f4ac7694-1767-588c-b12d-f501fe4f9050" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105640/selection/934173d437db32c5d1d10a5eaea13370839cf0031a002c20f9db6fb2f0aefe40" :answer-field/choices ["q-105640/selection/03da036926b8683a78d859bd5f9a652e7ef6f8083aa853853969df1fb1286c54" "q-105640/selection/541c51de94eca33dd95cb7f04cf4709a4b64a8774e7bf00da6cd38271004edfc" "q-105640/selection/934173d437db32c5d1d10a5eaea13370839cf0031a002c20f9db6fb2f0aefe40" "q-105640/selection/2cb876cf503485a55a0b4f0b4e5b3b54e8dd9ba62cbe32db7b046f0087139d2e" "q-105640/selection/0745f78343ab533087b71a60da3b79665cbfe6415b311709535e9e6adf213ebf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105640" :question/id #uuid "27fbdc78-f989-5a5c-ad92-84d3cb59b67e" :question/math-academy-id "q-105640" :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\cdot (2F+G)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF={e}^{5x}\\,i+y{e}^{3y}\\,j,\\,∇\\cdot G=3{e}^{5x}-2{e}^{3y}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (2F+G) & =∇\\cdot (2F)+∇\\cdot G \\\\  & =2∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{5x})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{3y}) \\\\  & =5{e}^{5x}+{e}^{3y}+3y{e}^{3y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (2F+G) & =2∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G \\\\  & =2\\cdot (5{e}^{5x}+{e}^{3y}+3y{e}^{3y})+3{e}^{5x}-2{e}^{3y} \\\\  & =10{e}^{5x}+2{e}^{3y}+6y{e}^{3y}+3{e}^{5x}-2{e}^{3y} \\\\  & =13{e}^{5x}+6y{e}^{3y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105640/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "78adaeaa-a91e-53e2-a192-1440d4d41211"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105640"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105635/selection/aa0dba5d54aef37ab5f7b38ad25e5c60e1ecf561c2862f2e796a4095a2476a2f" :answer/id #uuid "87aa8f2a-cd34-5e07-bf08-639b02ce5911" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(2+{y}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105635/selection/a9e36b6743f904525d7da55a141839d786224a2aed66832c08999df55255af1c" :answer/id #uuid "02a58f04-c260-5017-8312-72da3f94efa4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2y(1+2x+y)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105635/selection/6d98a41809b11960f7bdf18c135e3e5286fa79166b285bd6b792debdf4855fbe" :answer/id #uuid "3f02a394-2462-5fd1-bca8-aecdfca17dc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2y(1-y)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105635/selection/cd9407f62e73b0b7ed1029016d331d0f9908c791009fee2fb2f6c8b8ba66c8b7" :answer/id #uuid "c6077cff-b2a2-5f8f-a1a4-21ebd2b52da6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(2+x-y)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105635/selection/f4e5f00b978cc9ed790228108680f94016069d6d52e914b1a87aea3f354a7474" :answer/id #uuid "5d1bd6f5-b0e5-587b-ab7e-bc2bd95d7b1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(1-{y}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105635/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e7a25ad-d783-5194-8af2-5226b5ab2e86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105635/selection/6d98a41809b11960f7bdf18c135e3e5286fa79166b285bd6b792debdf4855fbe" :answer-field/choices ["q-105635/selection/aa0dba5d54aef37ab5f7b38ad25e5c60e1ecf561c2862f2e796a4095a2476a2f" "q-105635/selection/a9e36b6743f904525d7da55a141839d786224a2aed66832c08999df55255af1c" "q-105635/selection/6d98a41809b11960f7bdf18c135e3e5286fa79166b285bd6b792debdf4855fbe" "q-105635/selection/cd9407f62e73b0b7ed1029016d331d0f9908c791009fee2fb2f6c8b8ba66c8b7" "q-105635/selection/f4e5f00b978cc9ed790228108680f94016069d6d52e914b1a87aea3f354a7474"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105635" :question/id #uuid "6b6a087b-2c36-534b-953d-ce05fe481ed8" :question/math-academy-id "q-105635" :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\cdot (F-2G)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF={x}^{2}y\\,i+{y}^{2}\\,j,\\,∇\\cdot G=xy+{y}^{2}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (F-2G) & =∇\\cdot F-∇\\cdot (2G) \\\\  & =∇\\cdot F-2∇\\cdot G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2xy+2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (F-2G) & =∇\\cdot F-2∇\\cdot G \\\\  & =2xy+2y-2\\cdot (xy+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2xy+2y-2xy-2{y}^{2} \\\\  & =2y-2{y}^{2} \\\\  & =2y(1-y).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105635/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "78adaeaa-a91e-53e2-a192-1440d4d41211"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105635"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-105633"] :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}F)$ for the vector field $F$ where\n\n$$\nF=x{e}^{2x}\\,i-y{e}^{2x}\\,j+x{z}^{2}\\,k.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}F)=\\frac{1}{2}∇\\cdot F.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{e}^{2x})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-y{e}^{2x})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x{z}^{2}) \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}+2x{e}^{2x}-{e}^{2x}+2xz \\\\  & =2x{e}^{2x}+2xz.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}F) & =\\frac{1}{2}∇\\cdot F \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (2x{e}^{2x}+2xz) \\\\  & =x{e}^{2x}+xz.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-131298/selection/37ed1bbcc624e91066d47aa209d6c370c5e307c854f18d0ff7f6ac448013500e" :answer/id #uuid "5ebe5c3e-ebdf-5673-984a-53088c289103" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "yz\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+{x}^{2}{z}^{2}+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131298/selection/14710c6ecc165c3e87060e3c2a056355894460aafaf16e101747c980d2cf9a14" :answer/id #uuid "3b6b4720-5732-557e-8977-4705705a3876" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "xyz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+xz" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131298/selection/556e7a3e3fab0439b5c85f93fa95ab681d26b581fd34a6e43ba6db5af41924d5" :answer/id #uuid "d90f2d37-55fd-5d6e-8d94-fdfc0f8aaa92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+{x}^{2}{z}^{2}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131298/selection/e8cb5dfde41d36c2419affd42ac651c68daf35b9f745e58bf6eb584b614617f3" :answer/id #uuid "8906ddb3-4db1-5669-b584-b9ece9934cc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+x{z}^{2}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131298/selection/8865ac579ba189e2fb7e1a5c43f6282bcb48aca7f1b8efccf871e12013a05abf" :answer/id #uuid "655786a8-5a6d-5e8a-8195-dfbd2898fc6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+xz+2y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131298/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "40090188-1152-5e1a-9b85-59256fd4ef98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131298/selection/556e7a3e3fab0439b5c85f93fa95ab681d26b581fd34a6e43ba6db5af41924d5" :answer-field/choices ["q-131298/selection/37ed1bbcc624e91066d47aa209d6c370c5e307c854f18d0ff7f6ac448013500e" "q-131298/selection/14710c6ecc165c3e87060e3c2a056355894460aafaf16e101747c980d2cf9a14" "q-131298/selection/556e7a3e3fab0439b5c85f93fa95ab681d26b581fd34a6e43ba6db5af41924d5" "q-131298/selection/e8cb5dfde41d36c2419affd42ac651c68daf35b9f745e58bf6eb584b614617f3" "q-131298/selection/8865ac579ba189e2fb7e1a5c43f6282bcb48aca7f1b8efccf871e12013a05abf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131298" :question/id #uuid "03e52c39-e2e9-5af6-a354-a8cadad7ea37" :question/math-academy-id "q-131298" :question/problem "Given that $F(x,y,z)=⟨\\frac{4}{y}{sin}^{2}⁡z,x{z}^{2},\\operatorname{sin}⁡z⟩$ and $f(x,y,z)=xy+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨y,x,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡z⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{4}{y}{sin}^{2}⁡z)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{z}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡z)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & =(xy+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡z+⟨\\frac{4}{y}{sin}^{2}⁡z,x{z}^{2},\\operatorname{sin}⁡z⟩\\cdot ⟨y,x,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡z⟩ \\\\  & =xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+2{cos}^{2}⁡z+4{sin}^{2}⁡z+{x}^{2}{z}^{2}-2{sin}^{2}⁡z \\\\  & =xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+{x}^{2}{z}^{2}+2({sin}^{2}⁡z+{cos}^{2}⁡z) \\\\  & =xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+{x}^{2}{z}^{2}+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-131298/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "44d953c5-21bb-5326-bfac-e793cfe26cd2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131298"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-105651"] :question/problem "Given that $F(x,y,z)=⟨{e}^{3x},-2y{e}^{3x}⟩$ and $f(x,y)=2x,$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨2,0⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{3x})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-2y{e}^{3x})=3{e}^{3x}-2{e}^{3x}={e}^{3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & =2x({e}^{3x})+⟨{e}^{3x},-2y{e}^{3x}⟩\\cdot ⟨2,0⟩ \\\\  & =2x{e}^{3x}+2{e}^{3x} \\\\  & =2(x+1){e}^{3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-105645/selection/56ee69ada7ba261ac33a747287b09260e1d6a8df4b6c28088aa7c6ba17e50395" :answer/id #uuid "67c79333-9bae-5902-9675-e0f4098ea44b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{y}^{2}(y+2x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105645/selection/d817f56079ec62331a3984bafbf8350516d651dd61a8fdcbb4369b87e3756c3f" :answer/id #uuid "70a819c7-d226-5a52-b41f-ff5543b93252" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{y}^{3}+2x{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105645/selection/120895cab156dcf2be7547171cebc8a13751e6a7a2519c9d6fe3f32679fc4c1e" :answer/id #uuid "54200762-6c83-56c4-8878-49b72c97967c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x{y}^{2}(y+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105645/selection/5c2a1e4192c692c4d9f8f6fd4f718d8f20a8f4eeae973fed502540705add2501" :answer/id #uuid "c35f93f2-e9e1-5068-8807-37454ba1727b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{y}^{2}(y-x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105645/selection/5e7b636e611497b8ea32e2f1f7f42a19846c28e923c56ac33cbfd3e15bdfcd5e" :answer/id #uuid "95e03d98-2436-5c90-a62c-6c73490acf53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{y}^{3}-2x{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105645/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "82cffc9f-d07d-504d-a67e-7f2081a10473" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105645/selection/5c2a1e4192c692c4d9f8f6fd4f718d8f20a8f4eeae973fed502540705add2501" :answer-field/choices ["q-105645/selection/56ee69ada7ba261ac33a747287b09260e1d6a8df4b6c28088aa7c6ba17e50395" "q-105645/selection/d817f56079ec62331a3984bafbf8350516d651dd61a8fdcbb4369b87e3756c3f" "q-105645/selection/120895cab156dcf2be7547171cebc8a13751e6a7a2519c9d6fe3f32679fc4c1e" "q-105645/selection/5c2a1e4192c692c4d9f8f6fd4f718d8f20a8f4eeae973fed502540705add2501" "q-105645/selection/5e7b636e611497b8ea32e2f1f7f42a19846c28e923c56ac33cbfd3e15bdfcd5e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105645" :question/id #uuid "cba6a4de-5acf-50f2-bad3-204bca5298ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-105645" :question/problem "Given that $F(x,y)=⟨-{x}^{2},\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}⟩$ and $f(x,y)={y}^{2},$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨0,2y⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-{x}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2})=-2x+y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & ={y}^{2}(-2x+y)+⟨-{x}^{2},\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨0,2y⟩ \\\\  & =-2x{y}^{2}+{y}^{3}+{y}^{3} \\\\  & =2{y}^{3}-2x{y}^{2} \\\\  & =2{y}^{2}(y-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105645/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "44d953c5-21bb-5326-bfac-e793cfe26cd2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105645"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131288/selection/cdfd01cb31672219cc82bdc730bcb216db93b7e82f9d111aa729ecae090746e4" :answer/id #uuid "d9f79a40-1c5e-5873-8fb9-1e6755c0804a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(y+1){e}^{y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131288/selection/23d3c62fef5893ed8423f4c7ee423afbb9edec27cca94d90d533f2adac673f44" :answer/id #uuid "a00ac523-2255-5dd4-8726-ec1df28317ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(3y+1){e}^{y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131288/selection/2868931e0ffda91e914a0c7cdbbe65d2396f7402b4ba0e711a47117d1314e2c7" :answer/id #uuid "77fd1fa0-2431-5832-9fff-57834bf742ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(y-1){e}^{y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131288/selection/00971f52430bc9c1c71a5541b31a0081fb61a27c9cc241d1fc0cae179faae39e" :answer/id #uuid "7694bb3b-bd56-5fd2-8587-68b9d1b6ceda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(xy-1){e}^{y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131288/selection/9e27c0e7f1b9f422e86b4870149300f14625f0be111f8c9635c13f08cce411b0" :answer/id #uuid "ab4a3f7d-6d62-520e-a82a-eda2684beb51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x({y}^{2}+x){e}^{y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131288/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd151d94-a04d-5fde-9f4f-90064264cb5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131288/selection/23d3c62fef5893ed8423f4c7ee423afbb9edec27cca94d90d533f2adac673f44" :answer-field/choices ["q-131288/selection/cdfd01cb31672219cc82bdc730bcb216db93b7e82f9d111aa729ecae090746e4" "q-131288/selection/23d3c62fef5893ed8423f4c7ee423afbb9edec27cca94d90d533f2adac673f44" "q-131288/selection/2868931e0ffda91e914a0c7cdbbe65d2396f7402b4ba0e711a47117d1314e2c7" "q-131288/selection/00971f52430bc9c1c71a5541b31a0081fb61a27c9cc241d1fc0cae179faae39e" "q-131288/selection/9e27c0e7f1b9f422e86b4870149300f14625f0be111f8c9635c13f08cce411b0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131288" :question/id #uuid "6ebc4d7b-a3e8-5614-9da7-0eb086543f5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-131288" :question/problem "Given that $F(x,y)=⟨xy,y⟩$ and $f(x,y)=x{e}^{y},$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨{e}^{y},x{e}^{y}⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)=y+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & =x{e}^{y}(y+1)+⟨xy,y⟩\\cdot ⟨{e}^{y},x{e}^{y}⟩ \\\\  & =xy{e}^{y}+x{e}^{y}+xy{e}^{y}+xy{e}^{y} \\\\  & =3xy{e}^{y}+x{e}^{y} \\\\  & =x(3y+1){e}^{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-131288/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "44d953c5-21bb-5326-bfac-e793cfe26cd2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131288"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105647/selection/9c0bb5661d0b81d6abd00b37b29dfd8abf4122b2dc54ffaf5e87867b3a3d1495" :answer/id #uuid "cb349738-10e3-5433-9039-2d9734b9c31f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105647/selection/0a36315d2662dda2f33c8953fe799d7289c92f5dfdadd4f481ac2997b7f927b4" :answer/id #uuid "e568cc92-7e75-55aa-b46f-7531a356690a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3y(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105647/selection/d88ed0a3f07848f6b58229419bf34ab55c740c3d0489581a520cd37a8e593380" :answer/id #uuid "551ff15d-94c9-5471-a193-a9d651c03b64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105647/selection/01d38e3b5aa9094e0aaa726815d956d175b1a64f6f92c91bc59d61c645cb2763" :answer/id #uuid "909adcf5-1634-5aec-b763-2fdeecf7dd26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105647/selection/159533dadc2d74fa8cf1c337ed3610c40d61bd29ef259bd4ffa5ffa7898d8c9e" :answer/id #uuid "cf84ea4f-e8b6-59e1-9ad6-6bcd4adfd508" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105647/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4fea914f-0765-5a14-894d-009e1ae66f2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105647/selection/9c0bb5661d0b81d6abd00b37b29dfd8abf4122b2dc54ffaf5e87867b3a3d1495" :answer-field/choices ["q-105647/selection/9c0bb5661d0b81d6abd00b37b29dfd8abf4122b2dc54ffaf5e87867b3a3d1495" "q-105647/selection/0a36315d2662dda2f33c8953fe799d7289c92f5dfdadd4f481ac2997b7f927b4" "q-105647/selection/d88ed0a3f07848f6b58229419bf34ab55c740c3d0489581a520cd37a8e593380" "q-105647/selection/01d38e3b5aa9094e0aaa726815d956d175b1a64f6f92c91bc59d61c645cb2763" "q-105647/selection/159533dadc2d74fa8cf1c337ed3610c40d61bd29ef259bd4ffa5ffa7898d8c9e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105647" :question/id #uuid "db8cfe15-e125-5611-8818-211e5545d984" :question/math-academy-id "q-105647" :question/problem "Given that $F(x,y)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x⟩$ and $f(x,y)=3y,$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨0,3⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & =3y(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x⟩\\cdot ⟨0,3⟩ \\\\  & =9y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+0+12y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =21y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105647/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "44d953c5-21bb-5326-bfac-e793cfe26cd2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105647"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8742"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\nabla \\cdot (\\mathbf{F}-3\\mathbf{G})$ for the vector fields $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G,$ where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}=\\left(x^2+y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+ \\left(xy-y^2\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}, \\quad \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{G}=x+y.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $\\nabla \\cdot (k \\mathbf F) = k \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf F$\n\n- $\\nabla \\cdot (\\mathbf F + \\mathbf G) = \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf F + \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (F-3G) & =∇\\cdot (F)+∇\\cdot (-3G) \\\\  & =∇\\cdot F-3∇\\cdot G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{F}.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2x+x-2y \\\\  & =3x-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (F-3G) & =∇\\cdot F-3∇\\cdot G \\\\  & =(3x-2y)-3\\cdot (x+y) \\\\  & =-5y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8928"] :question/problem "Given that $\\mathbf F(x,y) = \\left\\langle \\dfrac 1x, xy \\right \\rangle$ and $f(x,y) = \\dfrac 1{x},$ calculate $\\nabla \\cdot (f\\,\\mathbf F).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\nabla \\cdot (f\\,\\mathbf F) = f\\, \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf {F}+  \\mathbf F \\cdot \\nabla f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf {F}$ and $\\nabla f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},0⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{1}{x})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy)=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+x)+⟨\\frac{1}{x},xy⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},0⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
